  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Tollen&#39;s reagent consists of a solution of silver nitrate and ammonia.</p><p>Terminal alkynes react with tollen&#39;s reagent and form white color precipitate.</p><p>With Tollen&#39;s reagent (ammoniacal <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>AgNO</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></math>), a white precipitate of silver salt is obtained.</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mo>-</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mo>&#8801;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mo>-</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><msub><mi>AgNO</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><msub><mi>NH</mi><mn>4</mn></msub><mi>OH</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo><munder><mrow><mi>Ag</mi><mo>-</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mo>&#8801;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>Ag</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>Sliver</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>acetylide</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>(</mo><mi>white</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>ppt</mi><mo>.</mo><mo>)</mo></mrow></munder><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><msub><mi>NH</mi><mn>4</mn></msub><msub><mi>NO</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></math></p>",
